WEBVTT

00:02.055 --> 00:04.088
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:06.935 --> 00:10.720
- You killed Naomi!
- She wants her people to come here.

00:10.772 --> 00:13.556
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

00:13.608 --> 00:16.142
If you want to live,
you need to come with me.

00:27.330 --> 00:29.072
- Who are you?
- Daniel Faraday.

00:29.124 --> 00:30.667
I'm here to rescue you.

00:30.709 --> 00:33.878
This is the team? These are the
wrong people for a mission like this.

00:33.920 --> 00:36.756
None of them have field experience,
military training.

00:36.798 --> 00:39.884
You can't drop them in unprotected.
There's only so much I can do.

00:39.926 --> 00:42.543
Where's the chopper?
Where did it crash?

00:42.596 --> 00:46.339
What kind of pilot do you think I am?
I put her down safe and sound.

00:46.391 --> 00:49.008
- Get up. You're coming with us.
- We need to stay where we are

00:49.060 --> 00:51.813
- so they can find us.
- See, there's your problem.

00:51.855 --> 00:53.481
We don't want to be found.

00:53.523 --> 00:56.307
You want to know why we're here?
I'll tell you why.

00:56.359 --> 00:58.893
We're here for Benjamin Linus.

00:58.945 --> 01:01.145
Now where is he?

01:21.468 --> 01:24.502
Did Ben mention knowing
anyone off the island?

01:24.554 --> 01:26.838
- You're sure of that?
- This is real simple.

01:26.890 --> 01:29.048
Do you know where he is, or don't you?

01:29.100 --> 01:32.103
- What do you want with him?
- I want to locate him.

01:32.145 --> 01:35.096
The people who hired me told me
his name's Benjamin Linus.

01:35.148 --> 01:37.640
They gave me this picture,
that's all he told me.

01:37.692 --> 01:40.309
They said find him.
And for what they're paying me,

01:40.362 --> 01:42.238
I don't need to know anything else.

01:43.114 --> 01:44.491
Do you?

01:46.076 --> 01:50.153
You want Ben? OK, he's with Locke
and your friend...

01:50.205 --> 01:51.863
- Charlotte.
- Charlotte.

01:51.915 --> 01:54.532
Locke's got her too.
We know where he's heading.

01:54.584 --> 01:58.713
Locke's the guy that killed Naomi.
Give me back my gun, Shephard.

01:58.755 --> 02:01.247
You want your gun back, I want answers.

02:01.299 --> 02:03.207
You don't trust me, I don't trust you.

02:04.928 --> 02:08.671
You're supposed to be dead.
Am I asking a billion questions? No.

02:08.723 --> 02:11.810
We both have the same problem,
this Locke guy.

02:11.851 --> 02:15.303
Even if Locke has your friend,
you can't waltz in there and grab her.

02:15.355 --> 02:17.889
- They're armed.
- How about that? So are we.

02:17.941 --> 02:20.808
- Why don't we move out...?
- You're not going anywhere.

02:20.860 --> 02:24.354
- Will that helicopter fly?
- It's what she does.

02:24.406 --> 02:27.492
- Then you can take me to your ship.
- Sayid, wait a second.

02:27.534 --> 02:30.787
We did call these people
to get us off this island, didn't we?

02:33.206 --> 02:35.000
Well?

02:35.041 --> 02:38.076
I burned a lot of fuel coming in.
I can't carry much weight.

02:38.128 --> 02:40.662
- I'll take three of you.
- In case you zoned out

02:40.714 --> 02:44.248
while tweezing your goatee, one
of these yahoos took Charlotte prisoner.

02:44.301 --> 02:46.417
I can bring her back safely.

02:50.473 --> 02:54.425
And if I do...
will you take me to the ship?

02:55.812 --> 02:57.095
Absolutely.

02:59.566 --> 03:01.808
You bring Charlotte back safe...

03:03.194 --> 03:05.478
...and I will take you off this island.

03:27.928 --> 03:29.961
- Good morning.
- Morning.

03:30.013 --> 03:33.548
It's a long walk to the next hole.
Do you need a ride?

03:33.600 --> 03:36.300
Thank you, but no.
My ball is right here.

03:36.353 --> 03:39.189
You're the first person I've seen
out here all morning.

03:40.440 --> 03:43.777
I believe we're paying quite a premium
for that kind of privacy.

03:43.818 --> 03:46.060
Indeed, we are.

03:49.115 --> 03:51.357
Is this your first time
in the Seychelles?

03:55.205 --> 03:56.529
I'd use the five iron.

03:57.582 --> 03:59.323
I think I'll stick with the seven.

03:59.376 --> 04:04.162
Tell you what. 50 euros says mine
goes closer to the pin with a five.

04:07.759 --> 04:09.334
Let's make it 100.

04:11.680 --> 04:14.432
Amazing, huh? How we wager.

04:14.474 --> 04:16.382
Makes just about anything more fun.

04:31.992 --> 04:33.316
Not bad.

04:33.368 --> 04:34.692
Not bad.

04:36.121 --> 04:39.697
So, what do you do for a living,
my friend?

04:40.625 --> 04:43.295
- I do nothing.
- Nothing?

04:43.336 --> 04:45.161
Doesn't pay for a vacation here.

04:46.006 --> 04:48.206
I was the recipient
of a large settlement.

04:48.258 --> 04:50.958
- Corporate merger?
- Actually a plane crash.

04:53.221 --> 04:55.672
Oceanic Airlines flight 815.

04:55.724 --> 04:57.757
I'm Sayid Jarrah...

04:57.809 --> 05:00.426
...one of the Oceanic Six.

05:04.357 --> 05:05.515
That's...

05:05.567 --> 05:07.600
That's amazing.

05:08.695 --> 05:11.020
I remember reading all about it.

05:11.781 --> 05:13.439
Take your shot, my friend.

05:26.630 --> 05:29.633
It appears you were right
about the five iron.

05:33.553 --> 05:36.389
Enjoy your round.
Don't worry about the wager.

05:37.390 --> 05:40.258
- It's all in good fun.
- No, you won. Allow me to pay you.

05:40.310 --> 05:43.146
- It's fine, thank you.
- I insist, Mr Avellino.

06:53.425 --> 06:55.833
"Is it free?" was the full extent
of my German.

06:58.638 --> 07:01.005
What are you looking for?

07:01.057 --> 07:04.092
I love Europe.
Everyone speaks English.

07:04.144 --> 07:07.512
- I'm looking for Potsdamer Platz.
- You don't need a map.

07:07.564 --> 07:10.014
It's one block down,
right across the street.

07:10.066 --> 07:12.058
Thank you.

07:16.364 --> 07:18.898
I'm Elsa.

07:18.950 --> 07:20.692
Sayid.

07:22.829 --> 07:24.737
Could I have an espresso, please?

07:26.249 --> 07:28.741
What sort of business
brings you to Berlin?

07:28.793 --> 07:30.451
I'm a head-hunter.

07:30.503 --> 07:32.047
A corporate recruiter.

07:33.340 --> 07:36.749
- And what do you do?
- My employer is an economist.

07:36.801 --> 07:39.293
He works in emerging markets.

07:39.346 --> 07:42.098
Actually, I don't really understand
what he does,

07:42.140 --> 07:45.477
which doesn't matter
since all I do is shop for him.

07:46.770 --> 07:48.511
And if this goes off,

07:48.563 --> 07:51.514
I'm at his side instantly.

07:51.566 --> 07:55.059
Which is wonderful, since he's only
in Berlin once or twice a year.

07:55.111 --> 07:58.855
Which is why you're enjoying
a luxuriously long midday coffee.

08:00.367 --> 08:01.743
Yes.

08:17.550 --> 08:19.208
Do I...

08:20.971 --> 08:22.597
...know you from somewhere?

08:23.556 --> 08:26.049
I'll tell you exactly where
you know me from...

08:27.769 --> 08:29.562
...if you let me take you to dinner.

08:43.285 --> 08:46.538
This is the restaurant
you're taking me tonight. 8.00.

08:47.998 --> 08:50.448
Well, if you can find it.

09:08.184 --> 09:10.145
- <i>Hello?</i>
- I made contact.

09:10.186 --> 09:11.511
<i>Good.</i>

09:29.664 --> 09:30.988
Take a look at this.

09:32.542 --> 09:34.419
Naomi had it with her.

09:36.046 --> 09:38.037
She was looking for Desmond.

09:40.550 --> 09:44.085
Whatever their real agenda is
it's clear they're not sharing it.

09:44.137 --> 09:46.337
Maybe Desmond
can shed some light on this.

09:48.725 --> 09:51.050
How long would it take
to get to the beach and back?

09:51.102 --> 09:52.343
Couple of hours.

09:53.730 --> 09:55.440
You mind?

09:55.482 --> 09:57.515
Anything I can do to help.

09:58.735 --> 09:59.851
Sayid.

10:02.614 --> 10:04.324
So how are we gonna do this?

10:04.366 --> 10:07.650
You know the best candidate
for this kind of mission.

10:07.702 --> 10:11.362
- And what kind of mission is that?
- I'll make Locke release Charlotte,

10:11.414 --> 10:14.167
and I'm going to do it
without any bloodshed.

10:14.209 --> 10:16.743
As opposed to the way I'd do it?

10:17.462 --> 10:20.382
The last time you encountered him
you put a gun to his head

10:20.423 --> 10:21.800
and pulled the trigger.

10:21.841 --> 10:23.875
That's not good diplomacy.

10:24.552 --> 10:26.377
Hey, Jarrah.

10:27.055 --> 10:29.672
You think you're going
after Charlotte without me?

10:29.724 --> 10:31.184
Of course not.

10:32.644 --> 10:34.354
Well, good.

10:35.772 --> 10:37.565
Is there anything else?

10:39.192 --> 10:42.560
- Yeah. Give me my gun back.
- We leave in ten minutes.

10:49.869 --> 10:52.153
Ready to give us a name, Gizmo?

10:53.415 --> 10:56.532
He's not gonna tell you who
his spy is on their boat, James.

10:56.585 --> 10:58.044
Yeah, and why not?

10:58.086 --> 11:00.536
Because that's the only thing
keeping him alive.

11:00.589 --> 11:01.663
Here's an idea.

11:01.715 --> 11:04.467
Why don't we take a gun,
point it to his big toe

11:04.509 --> 11:06.626
and send that little piggy to market?

11:06.678 --> 11:10.922
And if he still doesn't want to tell us,
we'll move on to the roast beef.

11:10.974 --> 11:14.227
- Why don't we do that?
- Then we have to carry him.

11:34.915 --> 11:36.656
John, how much further is it?

11:36.708 --> 11:39.742
- I need to feed Aaron.
- It should be here, the cabin.

11:41.254 --> 11:43.871
Maybe we got turned around.
Could be anywhere.

11:43.924 --> 11:44.998
No, it was here.

11:45.050 --> 11:47.583
What's in this cabin
that's so important?

11:47.636 --> 11:50.753
John's looking for somebody
to tell him what to do next.

12:00.941 --> 12:03.016
I guess I was mistaken.
It doesn't...

12:03.068 --> 12:05.737
It doesn't matter.
Plan's the same. We keep moving.

12:05.779 --> 12:07.437
The barracks aren't far.

12:07.489 --> 12:11.649
If her team is with Jack's group,
they know we're going to the barracks.

12:11.701 --> 12:13.693
Yeah, and Red here was wearing a vest,

12:13.745 --> 12:16.779
which means her posse's gonna come
expecting a gunfight.

12:16.831 --> 12:19.501
If all they want is her,
maybe we should let her go.

12:19.542 --> 12:23.672
I thought we were just gonna go hide.
Why do we need to take prisoners?

12:23.713 --> 12:25.538
Because she'll be valuable.

12:25.590 --> 12:28.843
- How is she gonna be valuable?
- He means as a hostage, love.

12:30.470 --> 12:33.390
- This is not what I signed up for.
- What did you sign up for?

12:33.431 --> 12:37.425
If we let her go, they'll look at it
as a sign of good faith.

12:37.477 --> 12:39.635
They'll look at it
as an act of foolishness.

12:39.688 --> 12:41.679
I'm trying to come up with a compromise.

12:41.731 --> 12:43.765
We're beyond compromise.

12:43.817 --> 12:46.736
And right now, Hugo,
I'm making the decisions.

12:48.113 --> 12:50.813
Is that going to be a problem for you?

12:57.956 --> 12:59.749
Kinda sucks, huh?

13:01.293 --> 13:02.533
What's that?

13:04.045 --> 13:06.079
Being told not to come along.

13:08.633 --> 13:10.667
Now you know what it feels like
to be me.

13:11.886 --> 13:14.723
Does that mean I should
wait 20 minutes and go anyway?

13:16.641 --> 13:18.018
Touché.

13:25.859 --> 13:27.892
You should go with them, Kate.

13:29.946 --> 13:31.771
- You're serious?
- Yeah.

13:35.243 --> 13:37.276
What, don't you trust Sayid?

13:38.121 --> 13:39.581
I don't trust Locke.

13:41.791 --> 13:45.128
What's preventing him from doing to me
what he did to Naomi?

13:48.548 --> 13:49.747
Sawyer won't let him.

14:02.812 --> 14:04.137
You got room for one more?

14:05.398 --> 14:06.973
Oh, yeah, she gets a gun.

14:08.443 --> 14:11.978
- The gun's a last resort, Kate.
- You give Locke that same speech?

14:12.030 --> 14:14.480
Hey! Let's move out.

14:23.375 --> 14:25.867
This guy, Sayid, where is he from?

14:27.754 --> 14:29.329
Iraq.

14:29.381 --> 14:31.091
Iraq?

14:32.467 --> 14:35.387
So he's just gonna go
and work everything out?

14:35.428 --> 14:37.462
What was he, a diplomat?

14:39.266 --> 14:40.381
No.

14:42.519 --> 14:44.177
No, he was a torturer.

14:56.116 --> 14:58.868
Naomi, were you close to her?

14:58.910 --> 15:01.152
Nope. Met her on the boat.

15:01.204 --> 15:03.957
You don't seem particularly affected
by her death.

15:03.999 --> 15:06.751
Sure, I'm affected. She was hot,
and I dug her accent.

15:06.793 --> 15:07.867
Nice.

15:08.628 --> 15:12.121
And this woman, Charlotte.
You don't care about her, do you?

15:12.173 --> 15:15.667
- Define "care".
- So much for camaraderie.

15:15.719 --> 15:19.087
Who's the one going after one
of their crash buddies with guns?

15:19.139 --> 15:21.464
Actually, I do care about Locke.

15:21.516 --> 15:26.094
Maybe you can tell me how he managed to
split your happy little family in half.

15:29.316 --> 15:33.101
There was a fundamental debate whether
your people came to rescue us...

15:33.153 --> 15:34.352
...or kill us.

15:35.822 --> 15:37.616
Which side did you land on?

15:39.367 --> 15:41.609
I'll let you know when I decide.

15:48.501 --> 15:50.535
You look fantastic.

15:53.173 --> 15:55.665
This is why I wanted to take you
to the opera.

16:01.097 --> 16:04.382
If a man can't wear his tuxedo
by the fifth date, why bother?

16:22.994 --> 16:24.371
You know what?

16:26.831 --> 16:28.656
I'm not bringing it.

16:29.292 --> 16:32.379
If tonight's the night he calls,
so be it.

16:37.550 --> 16:38.791
I'll carry it.

16:39.678 --> 16:42.795
If he does call,
I don't want you fired over me.

16:43.974 --> 16:46.924
You should tell your employer
there is newer technology.

16:47.602 --> 16:50.136
Oh, I've tried.
He's very old-fashioned.

16:50.188 --> 16:52.597
You know how bosses can be.

16:53.984 --> 16:55.694
Do you have a boss?

16:56.444 --> 16:58.478
Everyone has a boss, Elsa.

17:01.491 --> 17:03.524
Come on, we don't want to be late.

17:06.037 --> 17:07.914
Why are you still here?

17:07.956 --> 17:12.168
I mean, when we met, you said
you would be in Berlin for one week.

17:14.170 --> 17:17.424
The job I'm on is proving harder
to accomplish than I thought.

17:18.842 --> 17:20.958
Oh...

17:22.637 --> 17:23.836
...right.

17:24.931 --> 17:28.675
I was hoping it was because of me.

17:39.696 --> 17:41.072
Let's go.

17:41.114 --> 17:42.522
Strauss awaits.

18:20.779 --> 18:24.856
- What's his story?
- Daniel? Couldn't tell you.

18:24.908 --> 18:27.066
Half the stuff he says
goes way over my head.

18:27.118 --> 18:28.943
The other half goes way, way over.

18:29.829 --> 18:32.280
Frank, can I...?

18:32.332 --> 18:35.669
Sorry to interrupt. May I please
use the phone just for a sec?

18:35.710 --> 18:38.077
- For what?
- I want to call Regina on the boat.

18:38.129 --> 18:40.997
Since we're waiting
maybe I can just try to...

18:41.049 --> 18:43.750
- What is it, Daniel?
- I'd like to do an experiment.

18:43.802 --> 18:45.084
- Just...
- OK.

18:45.136 --> 18:47.889
You just keep it to that
science stuff, all right?

18:47.931 --> 18:50.631
If Minkowski gets on there,
hang up right away.

18:50.684 --> 18:52.508
Yeah, thank you, thank you.

18:53.728 --> 18:55.522
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Regina?

18:55.563 --> 18:57.357
Hey, hi, it's Dan. Hang on.

18:58.149 --> 19:00.266
- Can you hear me?
- <i>Yeah.</i>

19:00.318 --> 19:02.143
Yeah? OK. Hang on.

19:02.195 --> 19:04.864
I'm... oh... Yes.

19:04.906 --> 19:08.608
I am all set here. I have a fix.
Are you locked in?

19:08.660 --> 19:12.403
- <i>Getting your signal pretty clear.</i>
- OK, great, then.

19:12.455 --> 19:14.197
OK.

19:15.041 --> 19:16.449
Fire the payload.

19:16.501 --> 19:18.044
<i>Payload away.</i>

19:18.086 --> 19:21.621
Don't sweat it. He does this kind
of stuff on the boat all the time.

19:24.843 --> 19:27.377
<i>Forty kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:27.429 --> 19:29.796
<i>Thirty-five kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:29.848 --> 19:31.881
<i>Thirty kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:31.933 --> 19:34.300
<i>Twenty-five kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:34.352 --> 19:36.803
<i>Twenty kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:36.855 --> 19:39.608
<i>Fifteen kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:39.649 --> 19:42.736
- <i>Ten kilometres to beacon.</i>
- Regina?

19:42.777 --> 19:44.936
<i>Five kilometres to beacon.</i>

19:44.988 --> 19:46.364
<i>Zero.</i>

19:46.406 --> 19:48.147
I don't have it.

19:48.199 --> 19:50.358
<i>That's weird.</i>

19:51.995 --> 19:54.748
That is far more than weird.

20:17.103 --> 20:20.190
What's with the swing set?
These people had day-care?

20:20.231 --> 20:23.182
- You think they're here yet?
- Let's find out.

20:59.020 --> 21:00.730
It's coming from in there.

21:24.879 --> 21:26.287
Hurley, what happened?

21:28.174 --> 21:29.332
They left me.

21:31.011 --> 21:35.088
Locke's gone off the reservation, man.
He took this one chick hostage.

21:35.140 --> 21:38.226
He said Walt was the one who
told him to kill the other chick.

21:38.268 --> 21:39.894
- Walt?
- Dude, don't ask.

21:39.936 --> 21:44.065
I was trying to argue with him
so he would chill, but...

21:44.107 --> 21:47.058
How about you stop babbling?
Tell us what happened to them.

21:47.110 --> 21:48.653
Where are they?

21:49.487 --> 21:52.021
- Who are you?
- Where the hell did they go, tubby?

21:52.073 --> 21:55.483
Oh, awesome, the ship sent us
another Sawyer.

21:55.535 --> 21:57.193
Hurley, where did they go?

21:57.245 --> 22:00.415
Guess they were too busy tying me up
to tell me. I don't know.

22:00.457 --> 22:03.460
- So they all left? All together?
- Yeah. They were freaked.

22:03.501 --> 22:07.245
Locke said the people on the ship were
coming to rescue Charlotte and kill us.

22:07.297 --> 22:10.081
So... are you?

22:13.261 --> 22:14.544
Not yet.

22:16.556 --> 22:20.216
Did they say anything that suggested
where they were going?

22:20.268 --> 22:23.553
Locke said they were going
by Ben's house before they took off.

22:23.605 --> 22:24.887
Why would he go there?

22:24.940 --> 22:27.943
For all I know they could've
locked Ben in the closet too.

22:27.984 --> 22:29.225
Where's Ben's house?

22:35.909 --> 22:38.776
- You mind if I ask you a question?
- Shoot.

22:39.913 --> 22:42.030
Did the Red Sox really win the Series?

22:42.082 --> 22:45.033
Hey, don't get me started
on that, all right?

22:45.877 --> 22:48.369
My dad's from the Bronx.
I bleed Yankee blue.

22:50.382 --> 22:53.249
I can't believe it's been 100 days
since I've seen a game.

22:59.224 --> 23:00.965
It's the payload.

23:01.017 --> 23:03.009
It's finally here.

23:12.070 --> 23:14.739
- What is that?
- It's a rocket.

23:19.911 --> 23:21.288
Oh, no.

23:26.126 --> 23:28.003
Thirty-one minutes.

23:29.045 --> 23:30.589
Oh, no.

23:31.464 --> 23:32.664
This is not good.

23:35.594 --> 23:37.387
Your friends are back.

23:47.939 --> 23:49.514
Well...

23:51.735 --> 23:53.059
...look at that.

24:05.957 --> 24:08.908
Look for anything that might show
where they've gone.

24:08.960 --> 24:10.535
I'll start in here.

26:13.585 --> 26:15.618
Sayid!

26:19.507 --> 26:21.217
Don't worry, Kate's fine.

26:27.974 --> 26:29.382
Good job, Hugo.

26:30.644 --> 26:32.385
Sorry, dude.

26:36.232 --> 26:38.902
I'm sorry, Sayid. Nothing personal.

26:38.944 --> 26:42.197
- Where's Locke?
- Talking to that angry Chinese guy.

26:43.573 --> 26:45.533
I'm not going to hurt you, Hurley.

26:45.575 --> 26:47.775
Yeah. I saw you snap that guy's neck

26:47.827 --> 26:50.664
with that break-dancing thing
you do with your legs.

26:50.705 --> 26:52.165
I think I'll hang back here.

27:01.216 --> 27:03.249
Well...

27:03.301 --> 27:05.668
...I guess they're running out
of jail space.

27:11.393 --> 27:14.229
- I lost a dollar, you know.
- How'd you manage that?

27:14.271 --> 27:16.679
I bet John that you wouldn't be
stupid enough

27:16.731 --> 27:18.973
to fall for your friend as bait.

27:21.361 --> 27:23.478
What do you know about friendship?

27:24.239 --> 27:27.357
I know it's no use having friends
you can't trust.

27:35.417 --> 27:37.377
So I'm your prisoner?

27:38.086 --> 27:40.119
If that sort of thing turns you on.

27:48.597 --> 27:50.630
What are you doing here with Locke?

27:52.601 --> 27:54.759
- I'm not with him.
- Yeah, you are, James.

27:54.811 --> 27:57.136
- What are you doing with Jack?
- I went with Jack

27:57.188 --> 27:59.555
because I believe he can
get us off this island.

28:03.862 --> 28:06.396
Then I guess that's the difference
between us.

28:09.492 --> 28:10.952
I ain't lookin' to leave.

28:12.078 --> 28:13.788
Why not?

28:17.167 --> 28:19.867
'Cause I ain't got nothing
back there for me.

28:20.962 --> 28:23.663
And what's here that's so much better?

28:25.133 --> 28:27.625
Why do you want to go back, Kate?

28:29.179 --> 28:32.630
Seem to recall you being shuttled off
to jail before we landed here.

28:35.435 --> 28:39.178
So if you think there's anything
waiting for you other than handcuffs,

28:39.230 --> 28:41.900
then you really don't know
how the world works.

28:44.319 --> 28:47.937
Look around us, Freckles.
We've got roofs over our heads.

28:47.989 --> 28:51.858
- Electricity, showers, beds.
- How long, Sawyer?

28:51.910 --> 28:54.777
How long do you think
we can play house?

29:00.418 --> 29:02.535
Why don't we find out?

29:21.439 --> 29:22.597
Iced tea.

29:29.364 --> 29:32.367
- Thought you might be thirsty.
- I'm thirsty.

29:35.537 --> 29:37.779
I'm sorry about all the theatrics,

29:37.831 --> 29:40.448
but I didn't know
how many of you there'd be

29:40.500 --> 29:42.294
or whether you'd be armed.

29:42.335 --> 29:45.005
I had to cover my bases.

29:45.046 --> 29:47.007
What have you done with Miles and Kate?

29:47.048 --> 29:50.416
Kate's with Sawyer,
and Miles is somewhere else.

29:52.929 --> 29:54.170
He's fine.

29:54.222 --> 29:57.674
- All I did was ask him some questions.
- Did he answer any?

29:57.726 --> 30:00.051
- No.
- Did you have more luck with the woman?

30:02.897 --> 30:04.774
Not particularly.

30:06.151 --> 30:07.944
Why don't you turn her over to me?

30:07.986 --> 30:10.561
- Why would I?
- I agree these people are liars,

30:10.614 --> 30:12.939
and they're certainly
not here to rescue us.

30:12.991 --> 30:16.734
But if I return safely with Charlotte,
they'll take me to the ship.

30:16.786 --> 30:20.238
It's our best chance of finding out
who they are and what they want.

30:20.290 --> 30:23.241
Well, then, I can save you
a lot of trouble, Sayid,

30:23.293 --> 30:26.160
because Ben says
he's got a spy on the boat.

30:27.672 --> 30:29.132
Who?

30:29.174 --> 30:30.748
It's a secret.

30:32.052 --> 30:35.753
Forgive me, but the day I start
trusting him is the day I sold my soul.

30:37.057 --> 30:40.143
Give me Charlotte,
allow me to do things my way,

30:40.185 --> 30:43.761
or a war is coming which we
will both be powerless to stop.

30:43.813 --> 30:46.055
Why would I give you Charlotte
for nothing?

30:46.107 --> 30:48.474
I think you misunderstood me.

30:48.526 --> 30:51.446
I never expected you
to give her to me for nothing.

31:08.964 --> 31:11.800
- Should we get dressed?
- No.

31:14.219 --> 31:18.046
We're gonna have to get out
of this bed at a certain point.

31:19.182 --> 31:20.506
Why?

31:21.601 --> 31:24.093
Well, for one thing, because I know

31:24.145 --> 31:28.608
that eventually you're gonna have to go
to that job of yours, you know?

31:28.650 --> 31:31.601
The one you never talk about.

31:31.653 --> 31:34.270
There's nothing to talk about.
It's just a job.

31:37.826 --> 31:39.984
I know nothing about you.

31:42.581 --> 31:45.333
I understand you don't want
to talk about the crash,

31:45.375 --> 31:46.918
what happened to you.

31:47.711 --> 31:49.535
What about life now?

31:49.588 --> 31:51.298
What about you?

31:51.339 --> 31:54.540
It's what you do
when you're in love, right? You...

31:58.513 --> 31:59.889
In love?

32:04.102 --> 32:05.843
Yeah.

32:20.785 --> 32:22.110
OK.

32:24.581 --> 32:26.239
No more secrets.

32:30.754 --> 32:32.078
What do you want to know?

32:39.179 --> 32:41.713
He's here. My boss.

32:41.765 --> 32:44.966
I... I have to go.

32:45.018 --> 32:46.092
Now?

32:48.563 --> 32:49.804
Where?

32:54.235 --> 32:55.946
The Hotel Adlon.

32:57.155 --> 32:58.229
My dress.

33:08.500 --> 33:09.960
Elsa.

33:12.504 --> 33:14.329
You have to leave Berlin.

33:14.923 --> 33:16.122
What?

33:17.300 --> 33:19.876
- You can't be here anymore.
- What do you mean?

33:19.928 --> 33:23.046
- Why would I...?
- People will be asking questions soon,

33:23.098 --> 33:25.381
about what happened to your employer.

33:27.602 --> 33:30.053
And you can't be around
to answer them.

33:34.359 --> 33:35.683
My employer?

33:40.073 --> 33:42.273
This is about my boss?

33:46.246 --> 33:48.488
- Who are you?
- It had nothing to do with...

33:48.540 --> 33:52.158
The café?
You meant to meet me there?

33:55.130 --> 33:58.331
You used me to get to my boss.
What did you say?

33:58.383 --> 34:00.343
People will ask
what happened to him?

34:00.385 --> 34:03.054
- It's best you don't know.
- You're gonna kill him?

34:07.225 --> 34:09.258
You're gonna kill him?

34:10.145 --> 34:12.136
Do you even know him?

34:13.064 --> 34:15.765
- His name is on a list.
- A list? What list?

34:15.817 --> 34:18.017
- You have a list.
- It's my employer's.

34:18.069 --> 34:20.311
- Who is that?
- It doesn't matter who he is!

34:20.363 --> 34:23.617
You kill people 'cause they're
on a list? Innocent people?

34:23.658 --> 34:26.411
The man you're working for
is not an economist.

35:10.622 --> 35:12.332
What do you think you're...?

36:05.927 --> 36:09.097
Hey, I'm gonna ask you one last time.

36:09.139 --> 36:11.172
Why was Naomi
carrying this picture of me?

36:11.224 --> 36:15.009
You gotta understand something,
she was senior management.

36:15.061 --> 36:16.302
She stayed on her own.

36:16.354 --> 36:18.721
Naomi told me you people
were hired by her.

36:19.983 --> 36:23.069
So you look me right in the eye
and tell me

36:23.111 --> 36:26.145
you've never seen or heard
of Penelope Widmore.

36:35.415 --> 36:37.824
Fine. You don't want to tell me
the truth?

36:37.876 --> 36:39.502
I'll find someone who will.

36:39.544 --> 36:42.036
See, when that takes off, I'm on it.

36:48.303 --> 36:49.846
He's back.

37:09.240 --> 37:12.410
- Where's Kate?
- She decided to stay.

37:19.542 --> 37:21.743
- What happened to Miles?
- I traded him.

37:21.795 --> 37:24.495
- Traded him?
- I promised you Charlotte. Here she is.

37:27.592 --> 37:29.469
- You cheated.
- Did I?

37:29.511 --> 37:31.002
Yes, you did.

37:31.054 --> 37:33.838
Lucky for you that guy's nothing
but a pain in my ass.

37:35.934 --> 37:37.091
- Hey.
- Hey.

37:37.143 --> 37:40.480
All right. That gives us room
for one more.

37:40.522 --> 37:42.013
Charlotte?

37:42.065 --> 37:45.318
Go back? With all the fun
I'm having here? No.

37:46.278 --> 37:47.654
I've got work to do.

37:48.822 --> 37:51.022
Seat's yours if you want it, Daniel.

37:51.074 --> 37:55.120
No, thank you. I think I should
probably stay with Charlotte.

37:56.538 --> 37:57.737
All right.

37:59.207 --> 38:00.490
Frank.

38:00.542 --> 38:01.699
Frank?

38:01.751 --> 38:03.868
Just... just one thing.

38:06.089 --> 38:10.041
Just be sure that you follow
the same exact bearing

38:10.093 --> 38:13.044
that we came in on, OK?
No matter what.

38:13.096 --> 38:16.964
By that I mean no matter what.
Just... stay on it.

38:18.435 --> 38:19.509
Roger that.

38:29.195 --> 38:30.269
Be careful.

38:30.322 --> 38:32.480
I don't have to talk you out of coming.

38:32.532 --> 38:35.785
As much as I like helicopter rides,
you got this one under control.

38:37.704 --> 38:40.279
- Wish me luck.
- Good luck.

38:42.292 --> 38:43.866
Send me a postcard.

38:47.088 --> 38:48.965
You said we have room for one more?

38:50.050 --> 38:51.374
Yeah. Why?

38:53.595 --> 38:55.305
We should bring Naomi home.

40:36.364 --> 40:37.772
Take your shirt off.

41:00.597 --> 41:02.140
Is she dead?

41:04.100 --> 41:05.174
Yes.

41:07.270 --> 41:09.064
Why didn't she kill you?

41:12.400 --> 41:14.684
She was trying to get
information from me.

41:15.862 --> 41:17.238
What sort of information?

41:22.994 --> 41:25.445
She wanted to know who I worked for.

41:27.040 --> 41:29.323
She wanted to know about you.

41:30.085 --> 41:31.544
Of course she did.

41:35.799 --> 41:37.676
Why are you crying?
Because it hurts,

41:37.717 --> 41:40.335
or because you were
stupid enough to care for her?

41:43.390 --> 41:46.174
These people
don't deserve our sympathies.

41:46.977 --> 41:49.813
Need I remind you what they did
the last time you thought

41:49.854 --> 41:52.889
with your heart instead of your gun?

41:52.941 --> 41:55.725
You used that to recruit me
into killing for you.

41:55.777 --> 41:58.613
Do you want to protect
your friends or not, Sayid?

42:04.369 --> 42:06.402
I have another name for you.

42:11.042 --> 42:13.076
But they know I'm after them now.

42:20.010 --> 42:21.720
Good.
